# Docker Compose variables for the GPU half of a GPU SERVER deployment:
# modules/whisper and modules/ollama. Used ALONGSIDE config/server.env, which
# still holds everything about the server itself — this file only adds:
#
#   docker compose --env-file config/server.env --env-file config/gpu-server.env \
#       -f modules/event-bus/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/backend/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/eliza/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/vad-asr/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/emissor/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/whisper/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/ollama/docker-compose.yml up -d --wait --pull always
#
# (plus -f modules/reverse-proxy/docker-compose.yml on a public server).
# scripts/server-compose.sh adds both files, and this env file, by itself
# whenever config/gpu-server.env exists — that file's presence is what makes a
# checkout a GPU server.
#
# Like server.env, only values Compose needs before any container exists:
# image tags, the model file whisper-server is started with, host ports. Where
# the platform finds the two services is in config/custom.config.
#
# Nothing here is required: every value is the compose files' own default.

# Image tags. Pinned in the compose files; set these only to move off them.
# whisper.cpp publishes no release tags, only main-cuda-<commit> per build.
# WHISPER_TAG=main-cuda-d1be6fde11ac6e0407606b4e42fe72d34add8037
# OLLAMA_TAG=0.40.16

# The ggml model file in storage/whisper/ that whisper-server loads. Change it
# together with [cltl.asr.whisper_cpp] model in config/custom.config, and put
# the file there first (from huggingface.co/ggerganov/whisper.cpp).
# CLTL_WHISPER_MODEL=ggml-large-v3-turbo.bin

# Host ports, for an operator on this machine. Both bind to loopback by
# default; the platform reaches the services on the Docker network, and
# tenants reach Ollama through modules/reverse-proxy at /ollama/.
# CLTL_WHISPER_BIND=127.0.0.1
# CLTL_WHISPER_PORT=8090
# CLTL_OLLAMA_BIND=127.0.0.1
# CLTL_OLLAMA_PORT=11434
